@Tutorial(time: 30) {
    @Intro(title: "Explore an offline voice pipeline") {
        Trace synthetic PCM through codec, RTP, transport protection and separate MLS/DAVE examples.

        Build and run the offline VoiceBot package. Its public test-only keys, synthetic peers and invariant checks teach protocol composition; the program opens no device and never joins Discord. Never reuse fixture keys for real media.

        @Image(source: "LibraryArchitecture.svg", alt: "Application-owned lifecycle composes independent domain products, transport contracts and injected adapters.")
    }

    @Section(title: "Work through the VoiceBot example") {
        @ContentAndMedia {
            Open the [source package](https://github.com/CarsonAurum/DiscordKit/tree/main/Examples/VoiceBot) in your checkout. The listings are synchronized with the original example files. Preserve the directory layout when building the supplied package.
        }
        @Steps {
            @Step {
                **Adopt the independent media products.** Run `swift build --package-path Examples/VoiceBot`. The package selects portable media, codecs, Voice, VoiceCrypto, MLS and DAVE. A real network/device composition injects its own adapters and host ownership.

                @Code(name: "VoiceBot-Package.swift", file: "VoiceBot-Package.swift.txt")
            }
            @Step {
                **Inspect PCM, packets and RTP rollover.** Read demonstratePortableMedia() and main(). Bounded PCM streams are resampled with cumulative sample accounting. The packetizer crosses sequence/timestamp rollover, transport AEAD authenticates the RTP header, and a bounded jitter queue drains authenticated packets. Full frames are handled before/after packetization at the appropriate encryption layer.

                @Code(name: "VoiceBot.swift", file: "VoiceBot.swift.txt")
            }
            @Step {
                **Separate key establishment from transport.** Read the synthetic MLS exchange. Participant signing-key associations and expected external sender trust are supplied inputs; key establishment is independently adopted from transport ownership. Recovery may replace init/HPKE keys while preserving the related signing identity policy.

                @Code(name: "MLSExample.swift", file: "MLSExample.swift.txt")
            }
            @Step {
                **Inspect authenticated DAVE transitions.** Read the local DAVE demonstration with its bounded sender ratchet and epoch/transition behavior. A real session must authenticate signaling, participant membership and complete-frame transforms. Do not downgrade after an unverified or failed transition.

                @Code(name: "DAVEExample.swift", file: "DAVEExample.swift.txt")
            }
            @Step {
                **Run bounded local checks.** Run `swift run --package-path Examples/VoiceBot VoiceBot`. Expect local invariant output for PCM, codec components, MLS/DAVE and five authenticated packets. These results do not establish complete codec/MLS/DAVE interoperability, independent cryptographic review, qualified device routing or authorized Discord duplex media.

                @Code(name: "VoiceBot.swift", file: "VoiceBot.swift.txt")
            }
        }
    }

    @Assessments {
        @MultipleChoice {
            What does this offline round trip establish?

            @Choice(isCorrect: true) {
                Its named local framing, authentication and synthetic invariants.
                @Justification {
                    Protocol components and local peers provide scoped evidence. Live hosts, complete clients and physical audio routes require separate qualification.
                }
            }
            @Choice(isCorrect: false) {
                Production voice interoperability and physical-device qualification.
                @Justification {
                    Protocol components and local peers provide scoped evidence. Live hosts, complete clients and physical audio routes require separate qualification.
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
